{
  "name": "happy",
  "integration": "forescout-counteract",
  "description": "The primary path, POST /api/hosts/discovery, which selects properties inline in the request body so the whole estate costs one request per page instead of one per endpoint. The two-page walk here makes exactly three requests after login and the field index, and requests_absent proves no per-host GET /api/hosts/{id} was made at all; legacy-fallback covers the index walk instead. Page 2 is reached only by reading metadata.next_link off page 1, and the walk stops when page 2 returns no next_link.\n\nThe property document mirrors a recorded live one: hostname_calculated is the ONLY hostname it carries, so a field list without it imports no hostname from this deployment at all. lastSeenTS comes from the wrapper timestamp on `online` (1724839643), not from otsm_details_last_seen (1724826194), because the wrapper says when eyeSight last decided the endpoint was up and exists on every deployment; firstSeenTS comes from otsm_details_first_seen, the only first-seen the Web API has. os_classification is \"Unknown\" and must NOT become the OS. Host 169090600 arrives with its id in the address form the vendor sample shows and must still key on the integer the host index would have returned -- see id-stability-discovery and id-stability-legacy for the pair that pins that. sinceTime is absent because since_days defaults to 0.",
